      "exp_pt": "<h3>🎣 What to catch (Gear and baits)</h3><p>The European seabass is the second most popular fish (54%). It is caught from the shore with spinning. It is a predator that likes surf and foam.</p><p><b>Best baits:</b></p><ul><li><b>Sardine</b> — #1.</li><li><b>Shrimp</b>.</li><li><b>Worm</b>.</li><li><b>Squid</b>.</li></ul><p><b>Gear:</b> Spinning 2.4–3.0 m, reel 3000–4000, braid + fluorocarbon, hooks #1/0–3/0.</p><h3>🌊 Fishing conditions</h3><p><b>Swell:</b> 1–2 m, likes foam.</p><p><b>Wind:</b> West or southwest (brings food).</p><p><b>Relief:</b> Rocks, piers, river mouths, rip currents.</p><h3>🌓 When and why</h3><p><b>Season:</b> All year, peak — autumn and spring.</p><p><b>Time:</b> Dawn and dusk, especially on the flood.</p><p><b>Tide:</b> On the flood (first 2 hours).</p><p><b>Moon:</b> New moon and full moon.</p><h3>ℹ️ Important</h3><p>License required. Minimum size: 36 cm (Atlantic). Daily limit: 5 kg.</p>",
