      "exp_pt": "<h3>🎣 What to catch (Gear and baits)</h3><p>The white seabream is the most popular fish among amateurs (68%). It is caught from the shore with light spinning or float rod. It is a schooling fish, often near rocks and reefs.</p><p><b>Best baits:</b></p><ul><li><b>Shrimp</b> — #1, the most effective.</li><li><b>Worm</b> — works all year round.</li><li><b>Clam</b> — for larger specimens.</li></ul><p><b>Gear:</b> Light spinning 2.1–2.4 m, reel 2000–2500, braid 0.6 PE, hooks #6–1/0.</p><h3>🌊 Fishing conditions</h3><p><b>Swell:</b> 0.5–1 m, moderate.</p><p><b>Wind:</b> Any except strong north.</p><p><b>Relief:</b> Rocks, reefs, rocky bottom.</p><h3>🌓 When and why</h3><p><b>Season:</b> All year (closed Feb-Mar).</p><p><b>Time:</b> Day.</p><p><b>Tide:</b> On the flood.</p><p><b>Moon:</b> Full moon (best activity).</p><h3>ℹ️ Important</h3><p>License required. Minimum size: 15 cm. Daily limit: 5 kg.</p>",
